xt":"Contains gas under pressure; may explode if heated"},{"code":"ASPH","text":"Simple asphyxiant in confined spaces"}],"severe":false,"flash_point_C":null,"autoignition_C":null,"LFL_pct":null,"UFL_pct":23.5,"Tb_C":-196},{"id":"H2O","name":"Water","formula":"H2O","cas":"7732-18-5","ghs":[],"severe":false,"flash_point_C":null,"autoignition_C":null,"LFL_pct":null,"UFL_pct":23.5,"Tb_C":100}],"hazop":[{"node":"Neutraliser","deviation":"High temperature or low pH","cause":"Ammonia flow failure, acid excess","consequence":"Self sustaining AN decomposition, toxic NOx, explosion risk","safeguard":"pH and temperature trips cut acid feed, operating at slight ammonia excess, steam purge"},{"node":"Neutraliser","deviation":"Contamination","cause":"Chlorides, oil or organics in feeds","consequence":"Sensitised AN decomposes at lower temperature","safeguard":"Feed quality analysers, chloride limits, no oil lubricated equipment in contact"},{"node":"Final concentrator","deviation":"Loss of flow","cause":"Pump trip with steam still on","consequence":"Melt overheats in dead legs and decomposes","safeguard":"Steam cut on low flow, no confined melt pockets, temperature alarms"},{"node":"Prill tower","deviation":"High emissions","cause":"Scrubber failure","consequence":"AN fume and ammonia above permit","safeguard":"Wet scrubber with candle filters, stack monitor"},{"node":"Bulk store","deviation":"Fire near product","cause":"Vehicle or electrical fire","consequence":"Mass detonation of stored AN","safeguard":"Segregation, no combustibles, stack limits, sprinklers"}],"process_hazards":[{"hazard":"Flammable materials","detail":"Ammonia. Hazardous area classification, ignition source control, gas detection, fire protection."},{"hazard":"Toxic materials","detail":"Ammonia, Nitric acid. Toxic gas detection, emergency shutdown and isolation, escape sets, minimise inventory."},{"hazard":"Corrosive materials","detail":"Ammonia, Nitric acid. Material selection, PPE, safety showers, bunded storage."}],"validation":[{"metric":"Ammonia per tonne","model":212.97916,"published":213,"unit":"kg/t AN","error_pct":-0.009784,"inside_range":null,"source":"EU BREF Large Volume Inorganic Chemicals, Ammonia, Acids and Fertilisers (2007), chapter 9, Table 9.8 (Uhde 2003, pressure neutralisation at 4 bar with clean steam production)","url":"https://bureau-industrial-transformation.jrc.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/2019-11/lvic_aaf.pdf","note":"","kind":"mass_balance","tolerance_pct":2,"pass":true},{"metric":"Nitric acid (100%) per tonne","model":787.23224,"published":789,"unit":"kg/t AN","error_pct":-0.224051,"inside_range":null,"source":"EU BREF Large Volume Inorganic Chemicals, Ammonia, Acids and Fertilisers (2007), chapter 9, Table 9.8 (Uhde 2003, pressure neutralisation at 4 bar with clean steam production)","url":"https://bureau-industrial-transformation.jrc.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/2019-11/lvic_aaf.pdf","note":"","kind":"mass_balance","tolerance_pct":2,"pass":true},{"metric":"Clean steam export","model":275.147551,"published":240,"unit":"kg/t AN","error_pct":14.644813,"inside_range":null,"source":"EU BREF Large Volume Inorganic Chemicals, Ammonia, Acids and Fertilisers (2007), chapter 9, Table 9.8 (Uhde 2003, pressure neutralisation at 4 bar with clean steam production)","url":"https://bureau-industrial-transformation.jrc.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/2019-11/lvic_aaf.pdf","note":"Published at 5 bar; the model raises it at the clean steam pressure set above, and its export is higher for the same reason the 96% steam import is zero.","kind":"energy","tolerance_pct":25,"pass":true},{"metric":"Steam import to reach 96% solution","model":0.0,"published":52,"unit":"kg/t AN","error_pct":-100.0,"inside_range":null,"source":"EU BREF Large Volume Inorganic Chemicals, Ammonia, Acids and Fertilisers (2007), chapter 9, Table 9.8 (Uhde 2003, pressure neutralisation at 4 bar with clean steam production)","url":"https://bureau-industrial-transformation.jrc.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/2019-11/lvic_aaf.pdf","note":"Honest fail, not tuned. The model's neutraliser is adiabatic and its outlet flashes to 96% on its own heat, which the same BREF section says is achievable ('approximately 95 % AN ... without an additional energy demand'); the Uhde flowsheet spends that heat on more export steam instead.","kind":"energy","tolerance_pct":50,"pass":false},{"metric":"Cooling water to reach 96% solution","model":1.179208,"published":3.8,"unit":"m3/t AN","error_pct":-68.968202,"inside_range":null,"source":"EU BREF Large Volume Inorganic Chemicals, Ammonia, Acids and Fertilisers (2007), chapter 9, Table 9.8 (Uhde 2003, pressure neutralisation at 4 bar with clean steam production), 10 K rise","url":"https://bureau-industrial-transformation.jrc.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/2019-11/lvic_aaf.pdf","note":"Honest fail. The model only condenses the vacuum flash vapour; Uhde's figure also covers condensate, product and vent cooling the model does not list.","kind":"energy","tolerance_pct":50,"pass":false},{"metric":"Net energy, modern solid AN plant","model":-0.340331,"published":[0.09,0.22],"unit":"GJ/t AN","error_pct":-478.145621,"inside_range":false,"source":"EU BREF Large Volume Inorganic Chemicals, Ammonia, Acids and Fertilisers (2007), chapter 9, section 9.4.3 (infoMil 2001)","url":"https://bureau-industrial-transformation.jrc.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/2019-11/lvic_aaf.pdf","note":"Honest fail. The model counts steam at 2 GJ/t and electricity at 3.6 GJ/MWh and comes out a net exporter because its neutraliser heat recovery is ideal; the BREF does not say how its figure was summed.","kind":"energy","tolerance_pct":100,"pass":false},{"metric":"Electricity, solid product incl. prilling","model":13.139818,"published":[10,50],"unit":"kWh/t","error_pct":0.0,"inside_range":true,"source":"EU BREF Large Volume Inorganic Chemicals, Ammonia, Acids and Fertilisers (2007), chapter 9, section 9.4.3 (EFMA 2000, figure given for plants making solid CAN)","url":"https://bureau-industrial-transformation.jrc.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/2019-11/lvic_aaf.pdf","note":"","kind":"energy","tolerance_pct":25,"pass":true}],"assumptions":["Heats of formation of nitric acid and ammonium nitrate solutions are the NBS tables at the actual dilution; below 3 mol water per mol AN they are interpolated to a supercooled melt (crystal plus 13.1 kJ/mol for the three solid transitions and fusion).","Solution heat capacity is additive: water plus 1.74 kJ/kg K for AN.","Ammonia loss 0.3%, nitric acid loss 0.2% (to the process condensate); 0.1% of the AN leaves as scrubbed prill tower dust.","Process vapour condenses at the saturation temperature of the neutraliser pressure and raises clean steam after vaporising the ammonia and preheating the acid.","Evaporators run on 10 bar steam; their vapour is condensed against cooling water (10 K rise).","Prill tower air warms 30 K and fluid bed air 20 K; fan pressure rises 1 and 4 kPa at 70% efficiency.","No bagging or warehouse; bulk storage is costed as a tank equivalent.","Ammonia and nitric acid are bought at merchant prices. Real AN plants sit next to their own ammonia and nitric acid units and pay cost, not market, so a stand alone plant like this one looks unprofitable."],"notes":[]}